# Nuxt / Vue Conventions

## SFC style

- Always `<script setup lang="ts">`.
- Prefer Nuxt auto-imports (`useRoute`, `useAsyncData`, `navigateTo`, `useSeoMeta`, `createError`).
- Explicitly import from `~/data/*` and `~/utils/*` (project does this consistently).

## Component naming (path-prefix)

Folder under `app/components/` becomes the prefix:

| File | Usage in template |
|------|-------------------|
| `home/HeroSection.vue` | `<HomeHeroSection />` |
| `ui/AppButton.vue` | `<UiAppButton />` |
| `layout/AppHeader.vue` | `<LayoutAppHeader />` |
| `posts/PostCard.vue` | `<PostsPostCard />` |

Root-level components stay unprefixed: `ContactForm.vue` → `<ContactForm />`.

```vue
<!-- ✅ -->
<UiAppButton to="/work">View Work</UiAppButton>

<!-- ❌ Don't invent alternate names -->
<AppButton to="/work">View Work</AppButton>
```

## Pages & layouts

- Pages live in `app/pages/`; keep route SFCs thin — compose section components.
- Set SEO with `useSeoMeta` using `siteConfig` from `~/data/site`.
- Layouts: `default` only (header / main / footer + `container-site`). `/work` and `/contact` redirect to hash sections on `/`.
- Images: prefer `<NuxtImg>`; icons: Material Symbols (`material-symbols-outlined`).

## Reactivity

- `ref` / `reactive` / `computed` as usual; `defineModel` for two-way props (see `ContactSuccessModal`).
- Client-only DOM: guard with `import.meta.client`.
